    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <math.h>\\n\\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\\n\\n/*\\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\\n */\\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\\n\\n/*\\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in \\n * the system.\\n * The computation is tiled over i to improve cache reuse: for each\\n * tile of bodies we scan all j once and accumulate partial forces,\\n * preserving the exact per-body summation order (j increasing).\\n */\\nvoid body_force(Body * restrict p, float dt, int n) {\\n  const int TI = 32; // i-tile size: fits comfortably in L1 cache\\n\\n  #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\\n  for (int ii = 0; ii < n; ii += TI) {\\n    int imax = ii + TI;\\n    if (imax > n) imax = n;\\n    const int ntile = imax - ii;\\n\\n    float fx[TI], fy[TI], fz[TI];\\n    for (int t = 0; t < ntile; ++t) {\\n      fx[t] = 0.0f;\\n      fy[t] = 0.0f;\\n      fz[t] = 0.0f;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Scan all bodies j once for this tile of i's.\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n      const float pjx = p[j].x;\\n      const float pjy = p[j].y;\\n      const float pjz = p[j].z;\\n\\n      for (int t = 0; t < ntile; ++t) {\\n        const int i = ii + t;\\n        const float dx = pjx - p[i].x;\\n        const float dy = pjy - p[i].y;\\n        const float dz = pjz - p[i].z;\\n        const float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n        const float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n        const float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n\\n        fx[t] += dx * inv_dist3; \\n        fy[t] += dy * inv_dist3; \\n        fz[t] += dz * inv_dist3;\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Update velocities for this tile.\\n    for (int t = 0; t < ntile; ++t) {\\n      const int i = ii + t;\\n      p[i].vx += dt*fx[t]; \\n      p[i].vy += dt*fy[t]; \\n      p[i].vz += dt*fz[t];\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\\n */\\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading nbodie value\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading input values\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n\\n  return bodies;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\\n */\\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError writing to output\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\\n  int nbodies;\\n\\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\\n\\n  /*\\n   * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\\n   * and bodies' positions are integrated.\\n   */\\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\\n    body_force(bodies, DT, nbodies);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\\n      bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\\n      bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\\n      bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\\n\\n  free(bodies);\\n  \\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/nbody.c\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Tiling the i-loop and scanning all j once per tile improves cache reuse of body data, while OpenMP parallelization over tiles exploits the 4 cores. The exact floating-point summation order per body is preserved because each body's force accumulation still visits j in increasing order within its assigned tile.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Added restrict to enable compiler optimizations and hoisted p[j] coordinates into locals. Tile size TI=32 chosen to fit a block of bodies plus accumulators in L1 cache on ARM64. OpenMP pragma is ignored if -fopenmp is not enabled, leaving correct sequential behavior.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Cache blocking (tiling) over the i-loop with j-scan per tile\",\n    \"OpenMP parallelization over tiles (schedule(static))\",\n    \"restrict qualifier on body pointer\",\n    \"Hoisting p[j] coordinates into local variables\"\n  ]\n}",
